    <!-- Sub-page: matrix -->
    <string name="guide_matrix_p1">The Eisenhower matrix comes from an idea attributed to US president Dwight D. Eisenhower: “What is important is seldom urgent, and what is urgent is seldom important.” It helps you decide what to do — and above all what not to do right now.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_p2">It crosses two questions. Is it important? (does it truly serve my goals and values?) and Is it urgent? (is there time pressure, a deadline?). The answers place the task in one of the 4 quadrants.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_do">Crises and imminent deadlines, to handle first. E.g. hand in a file due tonight, call back an upset client.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_schedule">The core of meaningful work: goals, projects, prevention. Block time for it — this is the quadrant to cultivate. E.g. prepare an exam in 3 weeks, exercise, plan a trip.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_delegate">Urgent but low value to you: hand it off when possible. E.g. answer an email someone else can handle, book a taxi.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_eliminate">Neither important nor urgent: distractions and wasted time, to drop without guilt. E.g. aimless scrolling, pointless meetings.</string>
    <string name="guide_matrix_tip">The trap is spending your day in the urgent (Do and Delegate) while neglecting Schedule. Yet it is by cultivating Schedule that you reduce tomorrow\'s emergencies.</string>

    <!-- Sub-page: creating a task -->
    <string name="guide_create_p1">The + button captures a task in an instant (a title, a quadrant). “More options” opens the full editor. The editor saves automatically when you leave it — no button to forget.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_classify_t">Important &amp; Urgent</string>
    <string name="guide_create_classify_b">The only two toggles that set the quadrant. E.g. “Important” alone → Schedule; both → Do. The card takes the quadrant color live.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_due_t">Due date</string>
    <string name="guide_create_due_b">An optional date and time. The due date never moves the task: as it approaches, the task “pulses” and offers to make it urgent — your call. E.g. “Report” due Friday 5pm.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_label_t">Label</string>
    <string name="guide_create_label_b">A colored category, cutting across quadrants, to filter at a glance. E.g. Personal, Work, Home. Manage them from the Labels screen.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_rec_t">Recurrence</string>
    <string name="guide_create_rec_b">Daily, weekly or monthly. On completion the task stays on the board: its due date rolls forward to the next one and its subtasks get unchecked (so it doesn’t go to the archive). E.g. “Water the plants” every week.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_sub_t">Subtasks</string>
    <string name="guide_create_sub_b">A checklist within the task; the card shows progress (e.g. 2/5). Great for breaking things down. E.g. “Plan the birthday” → cake, invitations, decorations.</string>
    <string name="guide_create_ai_t">Reformulate (AI)</string>
    <string name="guide_create_ai_b">Tidies up the title, note and subtasks in one tap. Appears if an API key is configured (Settings → AI assistant).</string>

    <!-- Sub-page: day to day -->
    <string name="guide_daily_views_t">Grid or lists</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_views_b">Switch between the 2×2 grid and a vertical list per quadrant (in Settings).</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_search_t">Search &amp; filter</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_search_b">The magnifier icon at the top opens a search bar (title and note) and label filters — handy to find a task among many.</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_move_t">Moving a task</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_move_b">Long-press then drag to another quadrant (or to reorder). The ⋮ “Move to” menu does the same and stays accessible with TalkBack.</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_swipe_t">Complete / remove</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_swipe_b">Swipe right to mark done, left to remove the task from the board. Either way it goes to the archive — nothing is lost, you can restore it from there.</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_remind_t">Due-date reminders</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_remind_b">A task with a due date fires a notification as the time approaches (lead time adjustable in Settings → Reminders). Tap the notification to open the task.</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_widget_t">Home-screen widget</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_widget_b">Add the Kairós widget to your home screen to see the task count per quadrant at a glance. Tap it to open the app.</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_archive_t">Archive</string>
    <string name="guide_daily_archive_b">Every task that leaves the board is kept here, tagged “Done” or “Removed”. It is the only place to delete for good: restore a task, delete it permanently, clear all, or enable auto-purge after N days.</string>

    <!-- Sub-page: focus &amp; pomodoro -->
    <string name="guide_focus_focus_t">Focus mode</string>
    <string name="guide_focus_focus_b">“What now?” blends importance and due date to surface THE task to do now, plus a preview of what\'s next.</string>
    <string name="guide_focus_pomo_t">Pomodoro</string>
    <string name="guide_focus_pomo_b">A focus/break timer (e.g. 25 min focus, 5 min break) that survives closing the app, with a notification. Link a session to a task to credit its focus time.</string>

    <!-- Sub-page: AI assistant -->
    <string name="guide_ai_p1">Optional. Kairós can assist you via an AI model — handy to clarify, classify or break down a task. Each action appears in the editor when an API key is configured.</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_reformulate_t">Reformulate</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_reformulate_b">Tidies up the title, note and subtasks in one go (spelling, clarity, concision), without inventing anything. A “Restore original” button undoes it.</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_classify_t">Suggest classification</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_classify_b">From the title and note, the AI proposes the Important / Urgent axes — hence the quadrant. You stay in control: it\'s a suggestion, adjustable with one tap.</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_decompose_t">Break into subtasks</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_decompose_b">Turns a task into a checklist of concrete steps, appended after existing subtasks. Great to kick off a big topic.</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_keys_t">Providers &amp; keys</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_keys_b">Gemini (Google) or OpenRouter, with automatic fallback from one to the other. Enter a key in Settings → AI assistant (free tiers exist).</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_privacy_t">Privacy</string>
    <string name="guide_ai_privacy_b">Keys are stored encrypted on the device and never included in backups. Text is sent to the provider only when you trigger a reformulation.</string>

    <!-- Sub-page: theme &amp; backup -->
